WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.250 --> 00:00:01.943
In the Trobriand Islands,

2
00:00:01.943 --> 00:00:03.922
people sailed hundreds of miles

3
00:00:03.922 --> 00:00:05.984
to exchange shell ornaments.

4
00:00:05.984 --> 00:00:06.787
Not to keep,

5
00:00:06.787 --> 00:00:08.225
but to pass on.

6
00:00:08.539 --> 00:00:11.123
Necklaces travelled clockwise around the

7
00:00:11.123 --> 00:00:12.750
islands. Armshells,

8
00:00:12.750 --> 00:00:14.152
anticlockwise.

9
00:00:14.521 --> 00:00:16.111
Marcel Mauss built on it

10
00:00:16.111 --> 00:00:17.231
in The Gift.

11
00:00:17.231 --> 00:00:19.217
Gifts create three obligations: to

12
00:00:19.217 --> 00:00:20.363
give, to receive,

13
00:00:20.363 --> 00:00:21.675
and to repay.

14
00:00:22.352 --> 00:00:24.560
Marshall Sahlins named three kinds

15
00:00:24.560 --> 00:00:26.533
of reciprocity: generalised,

16
00:00:26.533 --> 00:00:29.079
balanced, and negative.

17
00:00:29.430 --> 00:00:30.607
Your turn.

18
00:00:30.607 --> 00:00:32.361
Who described it?
